{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 41, :comments ["He shall scrape — he shall peel, as in: יעשהו במקצעות. And in the Talmud: המקצע מכולן טפח." "After he has scraped — הקצות את הבית is an infinitive of the hif'il conjugation. From קצה one would say הקצו. But one may say: its meaning is the noun קיצוע, since it is written: אחרי הקצות את הבית — it follows that the scraping is called הקצות, for the expression is already written above: ואת הבית יקציע."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {1 "The lemma reads אשר הקצו, which is not the exact form in Leviticus 14:41 (אחרי הקצות את הבית); Rashbam himself quotes the full phrase אחרי הקצות את הבית in his discussion, so the lemma as transmitted may reflect a variant or abbreviated form."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:48:50.094111724Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}